    <p><strong>Executive Summary:</strong> This proposal outlines a comprehensive research initiative aimed at developing next-generation assistive technologies to significantly improve the quality of life for individuals with disabilities. The project focuses on bridging the gap between advanced robotics and everyday human needs through rigorous user-centered design.</p>

    <h2>1. Background and Rationale</h2>
    <p>While technological advancements have been rapid, many assistive tools remain fragmented or inaccessible to the general population. Current solutions often lack seamless integration into daily environments. To address this, we propose a study that draws inspiration from the legendary stability and structure of a <span class="highlight">constable</span>—one who ensures order and safety within a community—to create a framework where technology acts as a reliable guardian of independence for users.</p>

