    </div>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2023 Limerick Collection. Keywords: economist, bill, jurgen.</p>
    </footer>

    <script>
        const limericks = [
            "There was a young fellow named Bill,\nWho never could pay his own bill.\nHe ate up his lunch,\nAnd drank all his punch,\nAnd told his poor wife he was ill.",
            "Old Bill went to see a great bill,\nOf tax that he simply couldn't fulfill.\nHe called in a friend,\nTo help him amend,\nBut the math on it just didn't thrill.",
            "There once was a banker named Bill,\nWho thought that he'd make a good hill.\nHe put all his cash,\nIn a pile so massive,\nThat even a mouse found it still.",
            "Young Bill likes to wear a red hat,\nWhile trying to look very smart.\nBut when he walks out,\nWith his eyes shut tight,\nHe trips over his own two feet.",
            "There was a tall fellow named Bill,\nWho stood quite as high as a hill.\nWhen he looked at the sky,\nHe asked why it's blue,\nAnd answered himself with a chime.",
            "Old Bill loves to read books of lore,\nAbout history, past and before.\nHe reads them at night,\nBy candlelight bright,\nThen falls asleep on the floor.",
            "There was a man named Bill who was slow,\nAnd moved like a turtle in snow.\nHe tried to run fast,\nBut fell down at last,\nAnd had to walk home with a woe.",
            "Bill said to his cat, 'Meow, meow!'\nThe cat replied, 'You're a funny guy now.'\nThey played all day long,\nUntil the sun song,\nThen they both went off to their bow.",
            "There was a chef named Bill who could cook,\nWith dishes that made everyone look.\nHe made soup so hot,\nIt caused a small riot,\nAnd burned the whole kitchen nook.",
            "Bill went to the store to buy cheese,\nBut forgot what kind of cheese he should please.\nHe bought instead,\nA bag of red bread,\nAnd walked away with a sneeze.",
            "There was a poet named Bill,\nWho wrote poems filled with sill.\nHe wrote about cats,\nAnd rats, and hats,\nAnd then he wrote a book for kids.",
            "Old Bill loves to play chess,\nBut he always loses, I guess.\nHe moves his pieces wrong,\nAnd gets stuck in a fog,\nAnd ends up playing with his legs.",
            "There was a singer named Bill,\nWhose voice was loud and shrill.\nHe sang in the rain,\nWith a broken chain,\nAnd the birds flew away from the hill.",
            "Bill likes to swim in the lake,\nBut he hates the cold water shake.\nHe swims for a while,\nThen comes back with a smile,\nAnd says, 'I'll do it again tomorrow!'",
            "There was a farmer named Bill,\nWho grew pumpkins so big and full.\nHe sold them at fair,\nTo people everywhere,\nAnd made a lot of money, no doubt.",
            "Bill went to the gym to lift weights,\nBut he dropped the barbell on his toes.\nHe cried out in pain,\nAnd fell on the train,\nAnd missed his bus for the day.",
            "There was a teacher named Bill,\nWho taught kids how to build a hill.\nThey built it with sand,\nAnd watched it stand,\nThen the wind blew it down in a flash.",
            "Old Bill loves to ride bikes,\nBut he never wears a nice tie.\nHe rides through the town,\nWith a happy sound,\nAnd waves at everyone passing by.",
            "There was a doctor named Bill,\nWho saved lives with skill and will.\nHe cured the sick,\nAnd made them quick,\nAnd gave them a hug to feel good.",
            "Bill went to the beach to sunbathe,\nBut he got bitten by a gnat.\nHe rubbed his skin,\nAnd tried to win,\nBut the itch stayed there until midnight.",
            "There was a painter named Bill,\nWho painted pictures of a hill.\nHe used bright colors,\nAnd strange structures,\nAnd sold them for gold to a king.",
            "Old Bill loves to dance in the rain,\nWith a hat on his head and a cane.\nHe spins and he twirls,\nWith a happy swirl,\nAnd splashes mud on his pants.",
            "There was a lawyer named Bill,\nWho argued cases with a skill.\nHe won every fight,\nWith a clever light,\nAnd paid the judge a large sum.",
            "Bill went to the library to read,\nBut he found a book that was dead.\nHe opened the cover,\nAnd saw nothing there,\nAnd walked away with a frown.",
            "There was a musician named Bill,\nWho played songs on a violin hill.\nHe played a tune,\nSo sweet and soon,\nAnd the audience started to cry.",
            "Old Bill loves to fly kites,\nBut the wind is too strong tonight.\nHe tries to hold tight,\nBut the kite takes flight,\nAnd lands in a tree far away.",
            "There was a gardener named Bill,\nWho planted flowers on a hill.\nThey bloomed in the spring,\nWith a beautiful ring,\nAnd smelled like roses and mint.",
            "Bill went to the movie to see a film,\nBut he fell asleep on the rim.\nHe woke up at the end,\nWith a confused bend,\nAnd asked, 'What was that about?'",
            "There was a scientist named Bill,\nWho studied stars with a telescope pill.\nHe discovered a new planet,\nWith a glowing light,\nAnd named it after his cat.",
            "Old Bill loves to bake cakes,\nBut they always taste like mistakes.\nHe adds too much sugar,\nAnd makes it bitter,\nAnd serves them to his friends anyway."
        ];

        const container = document.getElementById('limericks-list');

        limericks.forEach((text, index) => {
            const card = document.createElement('div');
            card.className = 'limerick-card';

            // Split text by newline to create paragraphs
            const lines = text.split('\n');
            lines.forEach(line => {
                const p = document.createElement('p');
                p.textContent = line.trim();
                card.appendChild(p);
            });

            container.appendChild(card);
        });
    </script>
